    <item>
      <title>01 · Packet Triage</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/packet-triage/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/packet-triage/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;packet-triage&#34;&gt;Packet Triage&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#packet-triage&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; capture health → protocol hierarchy → conversations → candidate stream → exported evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/zeek/&#34;&gt;Zeek&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-preserve-the-input-and-establish-scale&#34;&gt;1. Preserve the input and establish scale&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-preserve-the-input-and-establish-scale&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#8fbcbb&#34;&gt;pathlib&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; Path&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#8fbcbb&#34;&gt;hashlib&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;p &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Path&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;traffic.pcapng&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;h &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; hashlib&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;sha256&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;with&lt;/span&gt; p&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;open&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;rb&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; source&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; chunk &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;lambda&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; source&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;read&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#b48ead&#34;&gt;1024&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#b48ead&#34;&gt;1024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        h&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;update&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;chunk&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;p&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; p&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;stat&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;st_size&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; h&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;hexdigest&lt;span style=&#34;color:#eceff4&#34;&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do not hash text output from &lt;code&gt;tshark&lt;/code&gt;; hash the actual input bytes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Wireshark, open &lt;strong&gt;Statistics → Capture File Properties&lt;/strong&gt;. Note interfaces, encapsulation, capture length, time range, and packet count. A snap length that cuts off application data limits extraction even if TCP headers are present.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>02 · HTTP / File Streams</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/http-streams/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/http-streams/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;http-requests-responses-and-objects&#34;&gt;HTTP Requests, Responses, and Objects&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#http-requests-responses-and-objects&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; identify the HTTP version → locate request → match response → decode transport framing → export object → inspect bytes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/burp_suite_community/&#34;&gt;Burp Community&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cyberchef/&#34;&gt;CyberChef&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/hxd/&#34;&gt;HxD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-find-the-actual-protocol&#34;&gt;1. Find the actual protocol&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-find-the-actual-protocol&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;http&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;http2&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tls&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tcp.port == 8080&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For plaintext HTTP on an unusual port, inspect the bytes for a request/status line, then use &lt;strong&gt;Analyze → Decode As → HTTP&lt;/strong&gt;. A port alone is insufficient.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tshark -r traffic.pcapng -d tcp.port&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;==&lt;/span&gt;8080,http -Y &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;http.request&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;HTTP/2 uses binary frames and stream IDs. A TCP connection can contain many simultaneous HTTP/2 requests. Match an HTTP/2 stream within its connection; a &lt;code&gt;tcp.stream&lt;/code&gt; value alone is not a single request.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>03 · DNS / Encoded Labels</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/dns/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/dns/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;dns-analysis-and-data-reconstruction&#34;&gt;DNS Analysis and Data Reconstruction&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#dns-analysis-and-data-reconstruction&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; queries and answers → suspicious suffix → direction → sequence/retries → encoding → exact bytes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cyberchef/&#34;&gt;CyberChef&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-inventory-names-types-and-answers&#34;&gt;1. Inventory names, types, and answers&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-inventory-names-types-and-answers&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dns&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dns.flags.response == 0&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dns.flags.response == 1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dns.qry.type == 16&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dns.qry.name contains &amp;#34;exfil.example&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Type 16 is TXT. Also inspect A, AAAA, CNAME, and unusual label lengths. DNS can carry data in query names or answer records.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tshark -r traffic.pcapng -Y &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a3be8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;dns&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; -T fields &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ebcb8b&#34;&gt;\&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  -E header&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;y -E separator&lt;span style=&#34;color:#81a1c1&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/t &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ebcb8b&#34;&gt;\&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  -e frame.number -e ip.src -e ip.dst -e dns.id &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ebcb8b&#34;&gt;\&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  -e dns.flags.response -e dns.qry.name -e dns.qry.type &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ebcb8b&#34;&gt;\&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  -e dns.a -e dns.aaaa -e dns.cname -e dns.txt &amp;gt; dns.tsv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inspect repeated field values before parsing an export as one-record-per-line. One DNS message can contain multiple questions/answers; the simple reconstruction helper assumes one relevant query name per exported line.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>04 · TLS / SSH</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/tls-ssh/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/tls-ssh/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;tls-and-ssh-metadata-before-decryption&#34;&gt;TLS and SSH: Metadata Before Decryption&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#tls-and-ssh-metadata-before-decryption&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; identify the session → inspect visible handshake → locate matching secrets → configure the correct decoder → verify plaintext.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/openssl/&#34;&gt;OpenSSL&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/openssh_session_key_recovery/&#34;&gt;OpenSSH key recovery&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/volatility3/&#34;&gt;Volatility&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-what-is-actually-visible&#34;&gt;1. What is actually visible?&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-what-is-actually-visible&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tls.handshake&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tls.handshake.type == 1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;tls.handshake.extensions_server_name&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ssh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A ClientHello can reveal supported versions, cipher suites, and server name when not hidden by encrypted ClientHello. TLS 1.3 encrypts handshake messages after ServerHello, including the certificate. Do not assume a capture always exposes the certificate.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>05 · TCP / UDP Sessions</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/tcp-udp/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/tcp-udp/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;tcp-and-udp-framing-state-and-exact-bytes&#34;&gt;TCP and UDP: Framing, State, and Exact Bytes&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#tcp-and-udp-framing-state-and-exact-bytes&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; establish liveness → identify framing → read banner → send exact message → interpret reply → keep the session through success.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/hxd/&#34;&gt;HxD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-separate-transport-failure-from-payload-failure&#34;&gt;1. Separate transport failure from payload failure&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-separate-transport-failure-from-payload-failure&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Observation&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Meaning&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Next action&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Connection refused&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;No listener / explicit rejection on that address&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Verify current endpoint&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Connect timeout&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Routing/filtering/unresponsive endpoint&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;One minimal liveness check&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;TCP connected, no bytes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;May be waiting for client message&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Read protocol/source before sending&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;recv()&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;b&#39;&#39;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;TCP peer closed its sending side&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Preserve bytes already read; classify EOF&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Socket timeout&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;No bytes within the chosen deadline&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Not equivalent to EOF or malformed payload&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;UDP receive timeout&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;No datagram observed&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;No proof of open/closed port or valid message&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If the user supplies a complete solver and a current endpoint, run that artifact before re-deriving it. If an instance expired, retry unchanged against the refreshed endpoint before changing the protocol assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>06 · Wi-Fi Capture Analysis</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/wifi/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/wifi/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;wi-fi-captures-with-the-approved-tools&#34;&gt;Wi-Fi Captures with the Approved Tools&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#wi-fi-captures-with-the-approved-tools&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; verify link-layer capture → identify AP/station → inspect security/handshake → use supplied key material → inspect decrypted traffic.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cyberchef/&#34;&gt;CyberChef&lt;/a&gt;. No aircrack installation is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-check-what-was-captured&#34;&gt;1. Check what was captured&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-check-what-was-captured&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;wlan&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;radiotap&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;eapol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A normal Ethernet capture from a Wi-Fi-connected computer may contain only already-decapsulated traffic. It will not necessarily contain 802.11 management frames, channel information, or the wireless handshake.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;Statistics → Protocol Hierarchy&lt;/strong&gt; and inspect the link-layer tree of a frame. Note whether the file contains radiotap + 802.11, Ethernet, Linux cooked capture, or another encapsulation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>07 · CAN / Cannelloni</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/can-bus/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/can-bus/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;can-bus-observe-decode-then-change-state&#34;&gt;CAN Bus: Observe, Decode, Then Change State&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#can-bus-observe-decode-then-change-state&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; verify interface → establish tunnel if supplied → record baseline → decode ID/data semantics → send one known frame → monitor the actual outcome.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/can_utils/&#34;&gt;can-utils&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cannelloni/&#34;&gt;cannelloni&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wsl/&#34;&gt;WSL&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-identify-the-provided-transport&#34;&gt;1. Identify the provided transport&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-identify-the-provided-transport&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Input&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Start&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;candump text log&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Parse timestamp/interface/ID/data offline&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;CAN PCAP/PCAPNG&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Inspect decoded CAN fields in Wireshark&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;SocketCAN interface&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;candump on the supplied interface&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;IP/port described as cannelloni&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Match UDP/TCP mode and return addressing&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Arbitrary custom TCP service&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Read protocol before treating it as raw CAN&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Classic CAN and CAN FD have different payload limits. A CAN identifier is not automatically a sender ID; its interpretation comes from the application protocol.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>08 · FTP / Mail / ICMP / SMB</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/protocols/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/protocols/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;other-protocols-find-the-data-channel&#34;&gt;Other Protocols: Find the Data Channel&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#other-protocols-find-the-data-channel&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; identify protocol → match control to data → reconstruct the correct direction → decode protocol content → verify the artifact.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/wireshark/&#34;&gt;Wireshark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/zeek/&#34;&gt;Zeek&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cyberchef/&#34;&gt;CyberChef&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/xxd/&#34;&gt;xxd&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-ftp-control-and-file-data-are-separate&#34;&gt;1. FTP: control and file data are separate&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-ftp-control-and-file-data-are-separate&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp-data&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp.request.command == &amp;#34;USER&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp.request.command == &amp;#34;PASS&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp.request.command == &amp;#34;RETR&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;ftp.request.command == &amp;#34;STOR&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Follow the control stream and inspect login/status codes.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Record the requested file and transfer direction.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Inspect &lt;code&gt;PORT&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;EPRT&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;PASV&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;EPSV&lt;/code&gt; setup.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Identify the corresponding data connection.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Save the data-channel direction containing the file, then inspect its bytes.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A directory listing is not a downloaded archive. The first FTP stream may contain credentials while a later connection carries the actual artifact.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>09 · Python / Ready Helpers</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/python-snippets/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/network-expl/python-snippets/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;network-python-helpers&#34;&gt;Network Python Helpers&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#network-python-helpers&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/python3/&#34;&gt;Python 3&lt;/a&gt; for scripts; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/tshark/&#34;&gt;TShark&lt;/a&gt; for packet parsing; &lt;a href=&#34;../../ajcbbc_allow_tools/cyberchef/&#34;&gt;CyberChef&lt;/a&gt; for visual encoding checks. Both downloads use Python&amp;rsquo;s standard library only.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Use an existing snippet only if the event permits prepared code. Keep the source offline alongside your notes and adapt endpoint/protocol values explicitly.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-downloads&#34;&gt;1. Downloads&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#1-downloads&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Helper&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th&gt;Input&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/snippets/network/session_client.py&#34;&gt;session_client.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;One persistent TCP conversation; exact send bytes; bounded buffered receive&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Host, port, JSON operation plan&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/snippets/network/dns_reconstruct.py&#34;&gt;dns_reconstruct.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Suffix-aware, ordered DNS data reconstruction&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td&gt;Bare qnames or final-column qname TSV&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Save the &lt;code&gt;.py&lt;/code&gt; files locally. A browser may display the source; use Save As or copy the full file. They do not require an online API, AI library, or packet parsing package.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
